P20 is finished: the "Where the yield went" section now follows premium §7.9 and §11.3. Typecheck and lint are clean, and `pnpm test` passes 302/302 across 50 files. P20 is ticked in `tasks.md` and the entry is added to `logs/progress.md`.

**What changed** (mainly `src/ui/charts/BinParetoChart.tsx`):
- **Card:** a white section card with radius 24 and padding 24 (16 on mobile). It holds the title "Where the yield went" with the SBIN/HBIN switch on the right, then "One bin holds 91.3% of the lost dies.", then the lot's yield loss as one big number, then the "Yield loss by bin" and "Share of all dies" labels.
- **Rows:** each row is 40 px high and shows the bin code (its name appears in a tooltip after 600 ms), an 8 px bar sized against the largest bin, the share of all dies, the die count, and a pill with the share of fails. The bar track, the cumulative tick and the detail line are gone. Six rows show by default, then "Show all N bins".
- **Bar colours:** only the top-loss bin is solid ember. The other bars are a pale grey with a thin outline. A selected row, whether clicked or linked from a finding, gets the selected fill and `aria-pressed`, and a selected non-top bar turns solid ink.
- **Empty state:** "No yield loss. Every die passed."
- **Copy:** five new `pareto.*` keys, two removed and one reworded. All 5 locales stay in parity at 236 keys, and the count in the parity test is updated to match.

**E2E:** I added `e2e/pareto-p20.spec.ts`, which checks A32 and A43 in light and dark, and updated `bin-pareto-task10` for the new row text. The related specs pass after a fresh build: Pareto, yield summary, findings, stats, verdict, vertical slice, editorial, loaded desktop and responsive, and typography. `editorial-p26b` failed once when run in a big batch and passed on rerun. Running it also rewrote an evidence screenshot in `logs/shots/`, which I restored. No visual snapshots changed.

**Decisions where the spec was silent or conflicting:**
- **Bin type switch:** §7.9 says the section should follow the wafer's display mode, but §11.3 says to keep the existing switch. I kept the switch, since §11.3 was written later for this task.
- **Big number:** it sits on its own line under the takeaway, labelled "Yield lost". That label is a new key, `pareto.lossLabel`, which §9.5 does not list.
- **Narrow cards:** below 448 px the die count column hides. Screen readers still get the count from the row's label.
- **Edge-Ring finding:** A32 expects this finding to select the matching row, but the finding cites no bin. A finding without a cited bin now selects the bin that holds most of its failing dies. This is a UI-only lookup and the report engine is unchanged.
- **Pill count-up:** the animated count on the pills is left for P28.

`logs/p26a.out` has 6 added lines that I didn't make, and the untracked `logs/p20.*` and `logs/prompt-p20.txt` files aren't mine either, so I left them all alone.[INFO] [KRS] <-- GenerateAssistantResponseCommand done totalEvents=207

